{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-143867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\n- $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n- ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n- $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-143867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition I is true. Every value of $f(x,y)$ in the table satisfies $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition II is false. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.5+0.1+0.1+0.2=0.9\\ne 1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is false. Because $f(x,y)$ does not satisfy condition II, it is *not* a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-143867" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2593e76e422fc7bb1e37da6fb58566d366c5e77c9286cc7866c1595c7f20b31a"} {"question" "q-143867" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Deve