/problem" "value" "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.16$ | $-0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.24$ | $0.35$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions is true?\n\n- $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1$ for all $(x,y)$ in $S$\n- ${\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1$\n- $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-143869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's check the given conditions:\n\n- Condition I is false. The value of $f(2,2)$ in the table does not satisfy $0\\le f(x,y)\\le 1.$\n\n- Condition II is true. Adding up all the values of $f(x,y)$ shown in the table, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y) & =0.2+0.15+0.16-0.1+0.24+0.35=1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Condition III is false. Because $f(x,y)$ does not satisfy condition I, it is *not* a valid probability mass function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-143869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2593e76e422fc7bb1e37da6fb58566d366c5e77c9286cc7866c1595c7f20b31a"} {"question" "q-143869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-143869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-143869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-110935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in {(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-110935" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)}) & =P((X,Y)=(1,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,2)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,2)+f(2,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.05+0.05 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jak