oper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(3,3)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(3,3)) \\\\  & =f(2,1)+f(2,2)+f(2,3)+f(3,3) \\\\  & =0.1+0.15+0.3+0.15 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2593e76e422fc7bb1e37da6fb58566d366c5e77c9286cc7866c1595c7f20b31a"} {"question" "q-111080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.45"] ["math" "0.55"] ["math" "0.65"] ["math" "0.7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.06$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,0),(1,0),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(1,0)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) \\\\  & =0.15+0.1+0.05+0.1+0.1 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2593e76e422fc7bb1e37da6fb58566d366c5e77c9286cc7866c1595c7f20b31a"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.05"] ["math" "0.25"] ["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.45"] ["math" "0.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=6) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,2),(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(1,4)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,6))+P((X,Y)=(2,6)) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(1,4)+f(1,6)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2593e76e422fc7bb1e37da6fb58566d366c5e77c9286cc7866c1595c7f20b31a"} {"question" "q-109337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.6"] ["math" "0.7"] ["math" "0.8"] ["math" "0.9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=2\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y\\le 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2593e76e422fc7bb1e37da6fb58566d366c5e77c9286cc7866c1595c7f20b31a"} {"question" "q-109336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.15"] ["math" "0.2"] ["math" "0.35"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.75"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-109336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,5),(4,1),(4,3),(4,5)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,5))+P((X,Y)=(4,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(4,3))+P((X,Y)=(4,5)) \\\\  & =f(2,5)+f(4,1)+f(4,3)+f(4,5) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111076" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2593e76e422fc7bb1e37da6fb58566d366c5e77c9286cc7866c1595c7f20b31a"} {"question" "q-111076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "q-111076" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/state.json" "file_sha256" "faca1b55fad52324514e08a54e4af7da2060f53f166468afd1cb6ee6f113a3fa"} {"question" "e-9126" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac a2$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $\\dfrac 52a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/example-9126.json" "file_sha256" "83f37d13971d1d37ec7e30988c3313f61caf3d4e510265e73b44fceaee237569"} {"question" "e-9126" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The support of $X$ is $S_X = \\{0,1\\},$ the support of $Y$ is $S_Y = \\{0,1\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS= S_X\\times S_Y = \\left\\{(0,0),  (0,1),  (1,0),  (1,1) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{(x,y) \\in S} f(x,y) = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(1,0)+f(1,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{2}+a+a+\\frac{5}{2}a & =1 \\\\ 5a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/example-9126.json" "file_sha256" "83f37d13971d1d37ec7e30988c3313f61caf3d4e510265e73b44fceaee237569"} {"question" "e-9203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\Big( (X,Y) \\in \\{(2,3), (6,1) \\}\\Big)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/example-9203.json" "file_sha256" "0cc334ec9a524c7aebcf66ffae1dcd26f8a7e27f0fe442090c28d01d54621dfa"} {"question" "e-9203" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(2,3),(6,1)}) & =P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(6,1)) \\\\  & =f(2,3)+f(6,1) \\\\  & =0.25+0.3 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/example-9203.json" "file_sha256" "0cc334ec9a524c7aebcf66ffae1dcd26f8a7e27f0fe442090c28d01d54621dfa"} {"question" "e-9204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\left( X\\cdot Y \\geq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/example-9204.json" "file_sha256" "734d99b667a52eb3a0b390e635d94858e8497995c13439e4a7c38110154dbe21"} {"question" "e-9204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\cdot Y\\ge 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,4),(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,4))+P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061806/example-9204.json" "file_sha256" "734d99b667a52eb3a0b390e635d94858e8497995c13439e4a7c38110154dbe21"}] "usage" {"q-109337" [] "e-9203" [] "q-109334" [] "e-9126" [] "q-109686" [] "q-109336" [] "e-9204" []} "basis" 1973 "retractions" [[17592186162212 :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y = 2$ | $Y = 4$ | $Y = 6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X = 2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nConsider the function $f(x, y)$ shown in the table above. Which of the following conditions are true?\n\n1. $0 \\le f(x, y) \\le 1$ for all $(x, y)$ in $S$\n2. $∑_((x, y) ∈ S)f(x, y) = 1$\n3. $f(x, y)$ is a valid joint probability mass function."] [17592186162224 :question/problem "|  | $Y = 0$ | $Y = 1$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X = 1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nCalculate $P(X = 0, Y = 1)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ shown in the table above."] [17592186162215 :question/problem "|  | $Y = 2$ | $Y = 4$ | $Y = 6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X = 2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X < 2orY = 6)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ shown in the table above."] [17592186162214 :question/problem "|  | $Y = 2$ | $Y = 4$ | $Y = 6$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X = 1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X = 2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P(X = 2andY \\le 4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x, y)$ shown in the table above."] [17592186161798 :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a$.\n\n|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac a2$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $\\dfrac 52a$ |"] [17592186161798 :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is\n\n$$\nS_X = \\{0,1\\}\n$$\n\nthe support of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nS_Y = \\{0,1\\}\n$$\n\nand therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS= S_X\\times S_Y = \\left\\{(0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1) \\right\\}\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$, we must have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{(x,y) \\in S} f(x,y) = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0, 0) + f(0, 1) + f(1, 0) + f(1, 1) &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{a}{2} + a + a + \\frac{5}{2}a &= 1 \\\\\n5a &= 1 \\\\\na &= \\frac{1}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186161808 :question/problem "Compute $P\\Big((X,Y) \\in \\{(2,3), (6,1) \\}\\Big)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.\n\n|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |"] [17592186161808 :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP((X, Y) ∈ {(2, 3), (6, 1)}) &= P((X, Y) = (2, 3)) + P((X, Y) = (6, 1)) \\\\\n&= f(2, 3) + f(6, 1) \\\\\n&= 0.25 + 0.3 \\\\\n&= 0.55\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186161809 :question/problem "Compute $P\\left(X\\cdot Y \\geq 4 \\right)$ given that 